{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>וְלֹא אָבָה, etc.</b> It uses the term אָבָה, which indicates unwillingness without reason, to say that even though he had no awareness of fear of Israel's passing through his city, and he was moreover confident in his heart that Israel had no power to do him harm — even so, he was unwilling. And this is what Scripture concludes: ״כִּי הִקְשָׁה HaShem״, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:31.173356571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}